125
00:08:21,173 --> 00:08:24,017
We had no need to retaliate
against your ugly bird.

126
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:29,041
But we needed to get our hands on that
little straw-haired friend of yours, you see.

127
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,700
The plan was simple.

128
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:33,197
We wanted to lure you both
into the jungle by having

129
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:36,104
your dear birdie here
squawk pitifully for help.

130
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,920
But the idiot refused to cooperate.

131
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:42,586
Now, you just call out
for your own opium now.

132
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:47,792
Give us a really loud squawk
and we might even let you go.

133
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,958
Alright, then we'll make you squawk.

134
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:56,060
Just call for the princess.

135
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,720
Call for help now!

136
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,256
Let's hear it, bird!

137
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:06,793
Call out to your beloved
princess, and this will all end!

138
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,313
Just open your mouth, you damn creature!

139
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,417
But then we realized
that little Straw Hat was

140
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,897
already neatly trapped
here just waiting for us.

141
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:18,862
In which case, we didn't
need that thing anymore.

142
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:20,250
Karoo?

143
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,540
What a dumb bird!

144
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:30,560
I'll kill you!

145
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:35,922
And were you the ones who planted
a bomb to injure the giant Dory?

146
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:37,500
Yeah, that's us.

147
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:38,876
Who is this new guy?

148
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:40,039
Is he on the list?

149
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:42,397
No, but he's clearly a friend of theirs.

150
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,897
Let's just get rid of him.

151
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:46,862
How dare you interfere
with a proud warrior duel!

152
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:47,860
It was you!

153
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:50,120
I'll kick your asses!

154
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,579
How about I get rid of you instead?

155
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,040
Oh, it's just so cute when
you find Miss Wednesday.

156
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:02,517
What's more, she really thinks she
stands a chance against agents like us!

157
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:04,460
Taste my peacock slasher!

158
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:05,720
I'll get you too!

159
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,000
Exploding Star!

160
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:11,300
Yeah, gotcha!

161
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:15,630
Wrong!

162
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:18,720
Nose fence and cannon!

163
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,560
Did you get burned? Usa!

164
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:30,040
10,000 kilograms? Press!

165
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:32,690
Now, now.

166
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,840
Let's calm down.

167
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:45,097
There's no need to get so
upset right now, Princess.

168
00:10:45,180 --> 00:10:47,239
We aren't planning to kill you yet.

169
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,860
We only came here to abduct you.

170
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:54,600
Those were Mr.

171
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:56,132
Three's explicit orders.

172
00:10:57,980 --> 00:10:59,060
Mr. Three?

173
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:01,060
The Wax Wax Fruit Man?

174
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:05,180
He's here on the island
with us! That's right. Mr.

175
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,536
Three the Candleman.

176
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:10,640
His body creates wax which he
can then control as he likes.

177
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,840
What's going on here?

178
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:16,940
Tell me!

179
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:20,857
Going on?

180
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,293
Of course it's lost on someone like you.

181
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:28,775
What's going on is that I'm creating
a work of art with your assistance.

182
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,318
Stand still like a good little girl.

183
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:38,937
Did you actually think
that someone like you could

184
00:11:39,020 --> 00:11:41,785
escape from an organization
like Baroque Works?

185
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:48,260
After all,

186
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,617
your friend over there has a big bounty on

187
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,171
his head and look at what happened to him.

188
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:54,510
Ha.

189
00:11:54,593 --> 00:11:57,237
Consider this our thank you for
what happened at Whiskey Peak.

190
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:00,837
You should learn to mind your own business,
you pathetic group of wannabe pirates.

191
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,657
It would be quite
beneficial to your health.

192
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:04,857
By the way, we have your swordsman friend.

193
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:08,637
And we've captured the other girl that
you brought along with you as well.

194
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:11,900
So you caught Zoro? Damn right.

195
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:15,139
In that case, you're in
more trouble than I thought.

196
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,441
Well, let's see how big you talk.

197
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:20,857
After one of my kicky bombs blows
up their little face of yours.

198
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:22,980
Try whatever tricks you want.

199
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,120
I'm gonna kick your ass.

200
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,740
This should be fun.

201
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:34,940
Mufi, no!

202
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:54,100
You weak little fool. Luffy!

203
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:57,700
No! Please! Luffy!

204
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,351
Let's go, Miss Valentine.

205
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:01,380
Usopp!

206
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:02,780
Cut out!

207
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:25,180
Damn you!

208
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,912
Struggling is pointless.

209
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,557
Once my candle jacket
solidifies around you,

210
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:34,522
