it's impossible to break through.

211
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:38,137
There's no denying that
you giants are very strong.

212
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:41,757
But once you've been captured, that
strength doesn't do you any good at all.

213
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,670
None.

214
00:13:42,753 --> 00:13:44,617
All that I had to do was use my brain.

215
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:48,377
There would be no sense in trying
to defeat you in a physical fight.

216
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:50,872
You were so busy enjoying your great win.

217
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:53,180
The capturing you is easy.

218
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:57,027
Don't glare at me like that.

219
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:58,768
It's positively terrifying.

220
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:02,237
You should be celebrating, shouldn't you?

221
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:06,379
At long last, your battle with Dory
the Blue Ogre has come to an end.

222
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:10,017
You fought on this island for a
hundred years for your precious pride.

223
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:13,657
Shouldn't such a long-lasting battle
make victory all the more sweet?

224
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:16,034
I mean, really, it's an accomplishment.

225
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:18,831
Even if it required a little outside help.

226
00:14:19,220 --> 00:14:22,120
Come on, give me a little smile. Shut up!

227
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,240
What would you know about this?

228
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:30,440
Of course, the real victor
in all of this is me.

229
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:37,897
The bounties placed on your heads
long ago remain in place to this day.

230
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,957
Today you're worth 200 million berries.

231
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,340
Quite a handsome son.

232
00:14:42,100 --> 00:14:42,930
Bounties?

233
00:14:43,013 --> 00:14:44,080
Big bounties.

234
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:47,102
I feel as if I've uncovered
a long-lost treasure.

235
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:51,300
so that's what you're after here mr.

236
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:55,997
three here's the girl
alabaster's sneaky spy

237
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:59,657
it's about time I was
positively sick of waiting.

238
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:01,517
You're full of nothing but dirty tricks.

239
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,757
I can't believe you!

240
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,997
Putting a bomb in Dory's
alcohol was low even for you.

241
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:08,537
What the barrels!

242
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,920
You did something to the
The drinks that I gave Dory?

243
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:16,480
Dory, how was your drink?

244
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,172
Hit the spot, didn't it?

245
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:22,340
Yes, it tasted almost godly, in fact.

246
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:26,000
No, that must be what Dory meant.

247
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:30,577
Hmm, you're an annoying little girl,
Princess, giving away our secrets like that.

248
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:31,895
But that's all right.

249
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:35,159
There isn't anything he can
do about it now, anyway.

250
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:37,730
CANDLE!

251
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,130
Mr.

252
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:52,867
Five, bring the swordsman
and the other girl.

253
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:55,240
Time to begin.

254
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,560
GIANT CANDLE!

255
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,360
What is that thing?

256
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:33,060
Here are the others.

257
00:16:38,380 --> 00:16:39,520
It's just sad.

258
00:16:42,380 --> 00:16:45,257
Idiots like these should have
been a lot easier for me to catch.

259
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,917
Should have caught them the first time.

260
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:47,830
How embarrassing.

261
00:16:47,913 --> 00:16:50,240
What is that thing? Nothing good.

262
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,080
I'm sorry, you guys.

263
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,280
But, Phoebe, what happened?

264
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:55,617
I thought you were with Luffy.

265
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:57,797
I was, but now...

266
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:02,233
If you're wondering about the straw
hat, I saw to that little runt myself.

267
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:05,565
Well, he didn't put up
much of a fight, either.

268
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:06,810
Right.

269
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:28,440
Welcome, one and all, to my
famous candle service set!

270
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:35,877
I guess this is what it feels like, to
be a candle stuck on a birthday cake.

271
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:38,078
Guys, what's that spinning up there?

272
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:42,320
I can't move. Great.

273
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:45,837
It's not surprising to me that
they don't want us moving around.

274
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:47,400
It's what captured means.

275
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,360
Damn, that stuff's hard.

276
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:56,887
And I can't put much strength
behind my swing from this angle.

277
00:17:57,580 --> 00:17:58,756
Something's falling.

278
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:03,880
I do hope you enjoy my candle service.

279
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:07,117
You may have noticed the wax
flakes that are falling from above.

280
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:10,377
You'll eventually be covered
and turned into wax figures.

281
00:18:10,460 --> 00:18:13,917
You'll become perfectly lifelike
statues for my collection.

282
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,877
Something that even I
couldn't achieve on my own.

283
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:21,431
I will literally capture your spirits
and encase them forever in wax shells.

284
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,485
It will be a true masterpiece.

285
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,880
You will die for my art.

286
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:29,387
I don't think so, you freak!

287
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:33,177
I have no interest in dying for
whatever it is you consider art!

288
00:18:33,260 --> 00:18:34,090
Hey, giant!

289
00:18:34,173 --> 00:18:36,137
Why are you laying there
doing nothing when you

290
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:38,897
could be beating the crap
out of this candle guy?

291
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:41,333
Now he is going to make one huge statue.

292
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:46,097
You can try to convince him, but
your efforts will be useless.

293
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,877
He's a little blue at the moment.

294
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:48,790
You see,

295
00:18:48,873 --> 00:18:50,597
he just realized how
unfairly he won his last

296
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,797
fight and he's lost
the heart to celebrate.

297
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:56,797
He killed his dear friend Dory with
whom he had fought for 100 years.

298
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:59,660
Dory was injured, but he didn't notice.

299
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:02,297
Just imagine how much pain
Dory must have been in.

300
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:03,851
He didn't stand a chance.

301
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:06,217
You did shed a few tears, though.

302
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:08,653
Perhaps you were crying for your friend.

303
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:10,160
Now it's no use.

304
00:19:10,340 --> 00:19:11,697
There's no one doing it.

305
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:13,839
He's dead, and it's all your fault.

306
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:26,000
I should have seen it. Huh?

307
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:28,860
I knew something strange was going on.

308
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:38,420
From the moment we first began to
fight, I knew Dory was hiding something?

309
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:40,462
but I couldn't tell what it was.

310
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:41,390
Hmm?

311
00:19:41,473 --> 00:19:42,731
You say that you knew it.

312
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,240
You're lying!

313
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:47,557
If you knew something was wrong,
why didn't you stop the fight?

314
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,797
Why didn't you give him a chance to rest?

315
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:53,998
I didn't see one tread of pity in
the way you ruthlessly cut him down.

316
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:59,097
You know nothing about honorable duels.

317
00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:02,300
Someone like you could
never understand my tears!

318
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:05,397
What do you know about the way of Elbath?

319
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:08,037
You think that I would shame a warrior?

320
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:12,414
Who hid the fact that he was weakened
so that he could continue to fight?

321
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:17,897
Only a truly great
warrior would go to such

322
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:21,100
lengths and such a man
isn't interested in pity.

323
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:28,200
Now, I know what really happened
and I must do something about it.

324
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:31,125
I'm going to finish this
with my own two hands.

325
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:42,019
That's the least I can do for Dory.

326
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:44,611
He was a great warrior and my dear friend.

327
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:49,810
Froggy!

328
00:20:57,780 --> 00:21:00,280
This chatterin' was gettin' on my nerves.

329
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,040
Usopp. Usopp.

330
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:12,500
They have to pay for this.

331
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:14,990
Oh, yeah.

332
00:21:15,073 --> 00:21:16,580
Those jerks have to pay.

333
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:28,120
You can't...take this either!

334
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:36,820
Alright, then it's settled!

335
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:39,360
Let's go beat them senseless!

336
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:40,710
Froggy!

337
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:42,960
Big fool!

338
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,140
It seems that I miscalculated.

339
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:49,577
I forgot how freakishly strong
these dumb giants can be.

340
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:53,700
It looks like you're going to
require more complete restraint.

341
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:56,060
Works, works!

342
00:21:57,560 --> 00:21:58,390
Handcuffs!

343
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:01,840
Still going!

344
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:10,640
And now for the finishing touch.

345
00:22:11,660 --> 00:22:12,600
Take this!

346
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:24,647
It'll be tough for you
to move now, won't it?

347
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,900
You really are despicable!

348
00:22:35,580 --> 00:22:38,500
Now, let's get these candles going faster!

349
00:22:39,100 --> 00:22:43,900
It's time to turn these people into
beautiful, artistic wax statues!

350
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:50,826
My chest is starting to hurt.

351
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:53,297
The wax is starting to get into our lungs.

352
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:57,027
At this rate, he's gonna turn
us into wax from the inside out.

353
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:58,830
That's it.

354
00:22:58,913 --> 00:23:01,137
Make it look like you're in
as much pain as possible.

355
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:02,102
That's perfect!

356
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:05,317
Expressions of agony are what
I seek to achieve in my art.

357
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:08,047
The finished product
will be simply splendid!

358
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:10,820
You must die filled with terror!

359
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:14,697
This is what you call art, you
creaky, weird-haired freak!

360
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:16,604
You guys are gonna regret this!

361
00:23:16,780 --> 00:23:18,577
You're gonna pay for what you did to Brook

362
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:20,657
and Dory and for what
you're trying to do to us!

363
00:23:20,740 --> 00:23:23,577
You can yell and scream all
you want to, little girl!

364
00:23:23,660 --> 00:23:25,072
No one can help you now!

365
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:33,010
A century.

366
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:46,820
For 100 years, Dory and I dueled day
in and day out, fighting endlessly.

367
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:51,400
We battled for our pride, as is
the way of the warriors of Elbath.

368
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:56,820
We fought with honor and with strength,
and still we are subjected to this!

369
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:59,020
Why has this happened to us?

370
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:04,540
Must we be forced to meet
our end in such a way?

371
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:05,660
Must we?

372
00:24:06,400 --> 00:24:09,997
It isn't fair for a warrior to
die such a dishonorable death!

373
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:12,440
Why can I not die in battle?

374
00:24:15,940 --> 00:24:17,060
Hold that look.

375
00:24:17,380 --> 00:24:18,400
Yes, that's it.

376
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:21,817
Such grief, such sorrow, and
just the right amount of anger.

377
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:22,730
How marvelous.

378
00:24:24,940 --> 00:24:26,200
Elbath, please.

379
00:24:27,660 --> 00:24:28,760
This isn't good.

380
00:24:29,020 --> 00:24:30,077
My hands won't move.

381
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:30,997
Can't we do something?

382
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:32,077
I don't want to die like this.

383
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:34,631
My body's already beginning to turn stiff.

384
00:24:34,900 --> 00:24:36,620
What are we supposed to do?

385
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,500
Zoro, do something.

386
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:40,130
Hey, Giant.

387
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:42,849
You can still move, right?

388
00:24:44,460 --> 00:24:45,620
Good. So can I.

389
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:49,641
I say we take them down together.

390
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,019
What do you think?

391
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,177
Hold on a second.

392
00:24:53,260 --> 00:24:54,378
What are you doing?

393
00:24:54,780 --> 00:24:56,977
Are you? Yeah. Quit messing around.

394
00:24:57,060 --> 00:24:58,537
You're not going to cut your own legs off.

395
00:24:58,620 --> 00:24:59,917
I'm not messing around at all.

396
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,617
It's the only way to get
us out of this situation.

397
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:03,637
Are you in or out?

398
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:05,257
Are you insane? No way!

399
00:25:05,340 --> 00:25:08,397
Even if you get down from here,
you won't get far without legs.

400
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:11,127
There's no way to know
for sure until we try.

401
00:25:11,500 --> 00:25:14,257
So are you saying you'd
rather just sit here and die?

402
00:25:14,340 --> 00:25:17,458
Why should we make it easy
for those guys to kill us?

403
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:21,876
Dying quietly without a struggle
doesn't make you any less dead, right?

404
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:23,317
The girl was right.

405
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,459
This guy's insane.

406
00:25:24,820 --> 00:25:25,650
He's bluffing.

407
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:27,957
There's no way he would do
something as crazy as that.

408
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:30,297
He's just trying to act tough
so his friends will feel better.

409
00:25:33,913 --> 00:25:35,860
That runt's got spirit.
I'll give him that.

410
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:37,727
He's doing better than I am.

411
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:40,765
I had actually begun to
lose the will to fight.

412
00:25:41,140 --> 00:25:42,260
Alright, I'm in.

413
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:43,980
Let's cut them to pieces.

414
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:48,537
You're not serious about this, are you?

415
00:25:48,620 --> 00:25:51,444
How are you planning on
fighting them afterward?

416
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:53,177
Who knows? But...

417
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:54,900
I plan to win.

418
00:25:56,500 --> 00:25:57,880
Who are these people?

419
00:25:58,100 --> 00:25:59,512
They're completely nuts.

420
00:26:00,380 --> 00:26:02,920
What kind of man is he, and why?

421
00:26:03,300 --> 00:26:06,357
Why do I feel like I've seen
that look somewhere before?

422
00:26:06,440 --> 00:26:10,640
Princess Vivi, sometimes it takes
more strength to live than to die.

423
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:13,120
Wait, I'll fight with you.

424
00:26:13,740 --> 00:26:14,570
What?

425
00:26:14,653 --> 00:26:15,740
Good, get ready.

426
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:18,220
And now, let's go!

427
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:22,341
Don't be foolish, what did
you want to accomplish?

428
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:36,005
When I get back, I'm
going to kick your ass in!

429
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,920
Let's get him, Usopp! Yeah!

430
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:45,240
The first guy!

431
00:26:46,780 --> 00:26:48,320
Loopy! Usopp! Kado!

432
00:26:48,760 --> 00:26:49,920
We're here, Froggy.

433
00:26:50,140 --> 00:26:52,797
Don't worry, we'll pick
up where you left off.

434
00:26:52,880 --> 00:26:53,820
Thanks, Usopp.

435
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,597
Beat them beyond recognition.

436
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:58,837
Show them expressions of pain
and agony they won't soon forget.

437
00:26:58,920 --> 00:26:59,750
Oh, I'm good.

438
00:27:00,380 --> 00:27:02,437
These guys messed up the best duel ever.

439
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:05,437
They're in some serious trouble
and they're gonna answer to me.

440
00:27:05,520 --> 00:27:08,417
So you're the one with the
highest bounty in the East Blue?

441
00:27:08,500 --> 00:27:10,617
My, how low marine standards have fallen.

442
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:12,288
It's almost tragic, really.

443
00:27:12,480 --> 00:27:14,080
Is that your hair?

444
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:15,097
You just shut up!

445
00:27:15,180 --> 00:27:17,500
Dude, it's on fire! Hush, you!

446
00:27:17,700 --> 00:27:18,877
Yes, he has weird hair.

447
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:20,317
Now, could you break this pillar?

448
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:22,871
We're about to turn into wax statues here!

449
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,637
Oh, are you guys in trouble?

450
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:27,132
Nope, no trouble at all.

451
00:27:27,300 --> 00:27:28,620
Wait, Zoro, your leg!

452
00:27:30,140 --> 00:27:32,257
Yeah, I made it about
halfway through, I'd say.

453
00:27:32,340 --> 00:27:33,497
And how exactly is that?

454
00:27:33,580 --> 00:27:34,639
No trouble at all!

455
00:27:35,340 --> 00:27:37,046
So, Luffy, what do you think?

456
00:27:37,180 --> 00:27:39,797
Could you go ahead and take
care of this pillar for us?

457
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:41,351
I think I've done enough.

458
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:42,960
Yeah, no problem.

459
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:44,870
Ha!

460
00:27:44,953 --> 00:27:45,840
I wouldn't be so sure.

461
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:49,700
I don't know what it
is, but let's break it.

462
00:27:49,940 --> 00:27:51,080
Right, let's do it!

463
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:54,595
Usopp, the brave warrior of
the sea, is ready to fight!

464
00:27:58,260 --> 00:27:59,240
Hurry, will ya?

465
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:00,580
We're dying here!

466
00:28:24,520 --> 00:28:26,217
Tries to be fast from leaving home.

467
00:28:26,300 --> 00:28:29,477
The factor behind our
back just keeps us strong.

468
00:28:29,560 --> 00:28:32,597
It's too bad cause
we're still selling for?

469
00:28:32,680 --> 00:28:34,277
It's so fun for ya!

470
00:28:34,360 --> 00:28:36,257
Just leave us alone.

471
00:28:36,340 --> 00:28:40,137
It may be for this
chasing impossible things.

472
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:42,597
But I just gotta try.

473
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:45,197
The crazier the dream!

474
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:48,720
The more ambition I'm gonna need.

475
00:28:49,320 --> 00:28:52,597
It may be for this driving home.

476
00:28:52,680 --> 00:28:55,997
But I know that I've just gotta fly!

477
00:28:56,080 --> 00:29:00,037
Far through the sea,
the great of paradise.

478
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:02,020
We've gotta fly!

479
00:29:03,180 --> 00:29:05,337
Don't give up, just keep on trying.

480
00:29:05,420 --> 00:29:07,596
And you'll see that you're closer to?

481
00:29:08,060 --> 00:29:10,280
The horizon of your dreams.
